# Explorer defaults to the live inferred view on open

## Context
The shared graph-source picker (`KgGraphSource`) restored the last stored source
from `sessionStorage` when the Explorer opened, so re-entering the Explorer could
land on a sandbox/asserted view the user picked elsewhere (Query/Chat) instead of
the live inferred graph. Requested behavior: opening the Explorer should default
to the live inferred view, not "the last one".

## Changes
1. `src/front/static/query/js/query-graph-source.js` — `wanted(explicit,
   forceDefault)` now returns `LIVE_INFERRED` instead of the stored value when
   `forceDefault` is set; `populate()` forwards `opts.forceDefault`. Resolution
   order on open becomes: explicit arg → `?simulation=` URL → **live inferred**
   (stored value is skipped). A deep-link `?simulation=` still wins.
2. `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js` — `_loadSimulationSelect`
   forwards `forceDefault`; the Explorer `init()` open path passes
   `forceDefault: true`. The legacy (non-`KgGraphSource`) fallback honors it too.
   Manual refresh (`loadSimulations()`) stays unforced, preserving the current
   selection; the Query/API page (`query-api.js`) is unchanged.

## Modified files
- `src/front/static/query/js/query-graph-source.js`
- `src/front/static/query/js/query-sigmagraph.js`

## Tests
Updated the JS-string assertions in `tests/units/front/test_kg_graph_source.py`
and `tests/units/front/test_explorer_simulation_select.py` (new
`test_explorer_open_defaults_to_live_inferred`).
`uv run --frozen pytest -q -m "not scenario"` → **9865 passed, 326 skipped**.

